cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OpenChemE: a verified open catalog for chemical engineering"
message: >-
  If you use this catalog, its templates, or its workflows in published work,
  please cite it. Cite the specific release you used, not the moving default
  branch, so the state you relied on is recoverable.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dai
    given-names: Kevin
    email: yu.dai@mail.utoronto.ca
    affiliation: University of Toronto
  - name: OpenChemE contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/laohei101/OpenChemE"
abstract: >-
  A curated, structured catalog of open-source software, datasets, and learning
  resources for chemical engineering, chemoinformatics, bioengineering, medical
  engineering, and adjacent fields. Records carry explicit verification tiers
  and dated evidence, so a reader can tell what has been independently checked
  from what has only been recorded. Ships with runnable engineering templates
  and reproducible computational workflows.
keywords:
  - chemical engineering
  - process simulation
  - open source
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - curated catalog
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
